From adfa5e11e2bec07f07bbdd08f811b4c75fa933c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:19:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: avoid a readiness query before APR
 callback registration

apr_device_probe() installs the service callback only after apm_probe()
returns. Querying SPF readiness inside probe therefore drops the valid
response and waits five seconds for nothing. The result is unused, and
q6apm_is_adsp_ready() already queries readiness for the PRM consumer.

Remove the ineffective query. Piano packet tracing confirmed the DSP
response was received and discarded because the callback was not ready.
This does not claim to fix the separate capture-triggered DSP watchdog.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
index 240d4a469ba..6066f0a02a1 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -901,8 +901,9 @@ static int apm_probe(gpr_device_t *gdev)
 
 	audioreach_set_apm_src_port(gdev->svc_id);
 
-	q6apm_get_apm_state(apm);
-
+	/* APR installs the response callback only after probe returns.
+	 * q6apm_is_adsp_ready() queries the state once replies can be handled.
+	 */
 	ret = snd_soc_register_component(dev, &q6apm_audio_component, NULL, 0);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to register q6apm: %d\n", ret);
